Q. Difference between restart and reload?

Restart completely stops and starts a service, which can cause a temporary service interruption. 
Reload only re-reads the service configuration without completely stopping the service, so existing connections are generally preserved. Not every service supports reload.

Restart = Stop + Start
Reload = Re-read configuration
